## 1. Grant

No right is granted to copy, modify, distribute, sublicense, sell, or
rehost any part of this codebase except as explicitly agreed in writing
by the project owner.

## 2. Pattern Provenance (legally bounded, honestly stated)

Royal Red was engineered from scratch. Where design patterns were studied
from open-source projects, the pattern was reimplemented natively and the
source cited in commit messages and the worklog. The legal record lives in
`rr-payload/reports` (LICENSE-AUDIT) and the worklog:

- **deepseek-harness** (MIT, (c) 2026 DeepSeek) — four primitives ported
  as direct pattern references: append-only event log, 5-layer policy
  waterfall, single LLM seam, declarative sandbox roots. MIT obligations
  honored: no warranty, attribution kept in citations.
- All other studied repos are PATTERN-ONLY (see LICENSE-AUDIT table):
  GPL/AGPL sources (Fooocus, stable-diffusion-webui) were never forked;
  the custom-licensed Open WebUI was never copied; the unlicensed
  AI-Resume-Generator was never touched (product is clean-room).

## 3. Third-party components

Runtime dependencies keep their own licenses (Next.js, React, Tailwind,
shadcn/ui, Prisma, Zustand, framer-motion, lucide — MIT/Apache family).
Their license files ship inside `node_modules` and nothing in this
repository alters their terms.

